{"id": "EUVD-2026-32870", "enisaUuid": "56bb1035-771d-3764-af10-3d64f9833d35", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nBluetooth: hci_conn: fix potential UAF in create_big_sync\n\nAdd hci_conn_valid() check in create_big_sync() to detect stale\nconnections before proceeding with BIG creation. Handle the\nresulting -ECANCELED in create_big_complete() and re-validate the\nconnection under hci_dev_lock() before dereferencing, matching the\npattern used by create_le_conn_complete() and create_pa_complete().\n\nKeep the hci_conn object alive across the async boundary by taking\na reference via hci_conn_get() when queueing create_big_sync(), and\ndropping it in the completion callback. The refcount and the lock\nare complementary: the refcount keeps the object allocated, while\nhci_dev_lock() serializes hci_conn_hash_del()'s list_del_rcu() on\nhdev->conn_hash, as required by hci_conn_del().\n\nhci_conn_put() is called outside hci_dev_unlock() so the final put\n(which resolves to kfree() via bt_link_release) does not run under\nhdev->lock, though the release path would be safe either way.\n\nWithout this, create_big_complete() would unconditionally\ndereference the conn pointer on error, causing a use-after-free\nvia hci_connect_cfm() and hci_conn_del().", "datePublished": "2026-05-28T09:35:19", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T19:26:43", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d41093723e47255d7d74df86e2736711c1b8486e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6823f730bf195fc296d9edd09e2ca94bc1ff5584", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1750a2df0eab61dc421a7afae74abdd239a44b85", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/dc34f8d8240f25dd137dc2758ebbcc75e3779142", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f8eaf92c57ad99358dd372580d5ff87623343a72", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0beddb0c380bed5f5b8e61ddbe14635bb73d0b41"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-46111", "GHSA-926m-qfg2-2w89"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "34f7307e-61fc-37c5-96f3-d15061c79f5c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.0"}, {"id": "4c3599d6-022b-3456-ab50-672bfbe270f4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "eca0ae4aea66914515e5e3098ea051b518ee5316 <d41093723e47255d7d74df86e2736711c1b8486e"}, {"id": "57445d28-2a3b-38fc-9cee-c37e9c1fef9c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "eca0ae4aea66914515e5e3098ea051b518ee5316 <6823f730bf195fc296d9edd09e2ca94bc1ff5584"}, {"id": "59ac8594-264d-36d4-bcc1-b07208c17a4e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.0.7"}, {"id": "75e4b1f8-d5f6-3051-8fcc-70d65a47fb29", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.90"}, {"id": "95f62c05-7f9c-3a20-9147-e1064ebb8615", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "eca0ae4aea66914515e5e3098ea051b518ee5316 <1750a2df0eab61dc421a7afae74abdd239a44b85"}, {"id": "9f8e2127-6091-3edd-928c-ce2b35569ce9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.32"}, {"id": "a25a4972-c1a0-3f58-81d4-f82e2d93a524", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "eca0ae4aea66914515e5e3098ea051b518ee5316 <0beddb0c380bed5f5b8e61ddbe14635bb73d0b41"}, {"id": "b0d517d9-e94d-36eb-ac1d-daa139c03d19", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "eca0ae4aea66914515e5e3098ea051b518ee5316 <f8eaf92c57ad99358dd372580d5ff87623343a72"}, {"id": "ce85e9c0-d33b-3288-8fba-679f7e3a1a74", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.140"}, {"id": "dbf9dbbc-ee4e-3af2-84cb-53778d688af2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1"}, {"id": "de3e3b72-203e-3b88-a2fe-8438e5fcafdd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "dec78719-4b7e-399f-901c-577ca53bba54", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "eca0ae4aea66914515e5e3098ea051b518ee5316 <dc34f8d8240f25dd137dc2758ebbcc75e3779142"}, {"id": "f341b006-de26-3105-a5c6-f0a0d3a80d9b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.183"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "91657b14-e885-3a70-8053-b1e52c5e0c73", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}